Article 5: When the People's Court adjudicates a case involving major disputes among shareholders of a limited liability company, it shall emphasize mediation. Where the parties reach a consensus to resolve the disputes in the following manners, and such manners do not violate the mandatory provisions of laws or administrative regulations, the People's Court shall support them:
(1) The company repurchases shares of some shareholders;
(2) Other shareholders acquire shares of some shareholders;
(3) A third party acquires shares of some shareholders;
(4) The company reduces its registered capital;
(5) The company splits;
(6) Other manners that can resolve the disputes, restore the normal operation of the company, and avoid the dissolution of the company.
